;; Direct development-hook configuration.
;;
;; bin/seon-hook runs in Babashka. Syntax validation (clj-kondo over the
;; reconstructed buffer) happens before an edit; clj-kondo, the canonical
;; Markdown and docstring linters run after it. The one live-JVM call is
;; the contract compile check (`:contract-compile`, on unless declared
;; off): a src/ or test/ Clojure edit asks the running root at
;; `:current-source` to compile its contracts, and reports it unavailable
;; when no root answers. The hook never publishes: every JVM runs a
;; committed archive, so program changes reach default only as commits, by
;; `bin/seon start --head` (owner 2026-09-26). The only automatic fix is
;; Markdown formatting (whitespace, blank lines, final newline), which the
;; hook rewrites in place and reports; Clojure is refused, never repaired.
;; The review sizes and call bound below refuse by key path when absent;
;; `:feedback :max-tokens` (per message) and `:interval-seconds` still
;; carry literal fallbacks in bin/seon-hook.
;; SEON_HOOK_CONFIG selects a complete fixture config.

{:lint
 {:enabled true}

 :markdown-lint
 {:enabled true}

 :docstring-lint
 {:enabled true}

 ;; Writes no tool payload names. A shell tool — `apply_patch` from a
 ;; heredoc, `python`, `sed`, `cat >` — hands the hook no path, so the
 ;; changed files are derived: every root below is walked after the tool
 ;; returns and each Clojure file's content digest is compared with the
 ;; digest this session's agent recorded before the tool ran. A syntax
 ;; error left on disk blocks immediately, naming the path and the tool.
 ;; Measured 2026-09-25: the walk plus digests is 60 ms over 693 files,
 ;; where scoping by `git status --porcelain` cost 2.7 s warm (2026-09-17).
 :shell-writes
 {:enabled true
  :roots ["src" "test" "resources" "script" "bin"]}

 ;; These two keys select the live root and cluster that schema/contract
 ;; lint queries; the hook publishes nothing into it.
 :current-source
 {:root "."
  :cluster "default"}

 ;; The standing review rubric is DATA: `:skills` names skill directories
 ;; under `.agents/skills/`, each of whose `SKILL.md` is read fresh on every
 ;; review (edit a skill and the next review sees it — nothing is baked in),
 ;; review. The selection is the subset with real catch-power for a reviewer
 ;; of the current JVM/Clojure tree; the pod-era
 ;; skills (clojurescript, datastar-web-ui, ui-canvas, seon-context-config)
 ;; and the agent-REPL skill are deliberately absent.
 ;; OFF (2026-09-25): the owner's standing rule is no provider call that is
 ;; not a deliberate verification, and each window is one `agy` call. The
 ;; batch had in fact been dead since 72fa85fc3 (2026-09-22): the worker
 ;; admission threw on a missing worker record. Turning it on is the
 ;; owner's call; the output lands only in `tmp/reviews/`, never in the
 ;; editing agent's context.
 :review
 {:enabled false
  :interval-seconds 120
  :skills ["data-oriented-clojure" "data-modeling" "datahike" "clojure-testing"]
  ;; Per-document caps. Clojure sources under `:max-code-length` arrive
  ;; WHOLE, which is what stops a reviewer reading a cut as a syntax error;
  ;; anything longer is cut with an in-band truncation marker.
  :max-code-length 40000
  :max-batch-length 200000
  :max-rubric-length 60000
  ;; The provider call's own declared bound. One review window waits at most
  ;; this long; a fired bound drops the snapshot and is logged, never retried.
  :call-timeout-seconds 60}

 ;; 2026-09-20 (owner): schema admission spawned a full clojure -M:dev JVM per
 ;; schema resource edit; OFF until it runs through the live JVM or Babashka.
 :schema-admission
 {:enabled false}

 :feedback
 {:max-tokens 300}}
